            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request correctly modifies the `generate` function to respect the `max_tokens` parameter if it's provided in `sampling_params`, falling back to a default value otherwise. The logic is sound. I have one suggestion to make the code slightly more idiomatic and efficient, consistent with how other parameters are handled in the same function.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile this line correctly sets a default value for `max_tokens` if it's not already in `sampling_params`, using `dict.setdefault()` is more idiomatic and slightly more efficient for this purpose. It achieves the same result with a single dictionary operation and would be consistent with how `repetition_penalty` is handled just two lines below.\n\n```suggestion\n        sampling_params.setdefault(\"max_tokens\", self.config.max_model_len - len(prompt_ids))\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2025-11-19T11:56:23Z",
                  "databaseId": 2541693901,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -379,10 +379,10 @@ async def generate(\n     ) -> TokenOutput:\n         \"\"\"Generate sequence with token-in-token-out.\"\"\"\n         # TODO(@wuxibin): switch to `/generate` http endpoint once multi-modal support ready.\n-        max_tokens = self.config.max_model_len - len(prompt_ids)\n+        sampling_params[\"max_tokens\"] = sampling_params.pop(\"max_tokens\", self.config.max_model_len - len(prompt_ids))",
